The deferred GAP-ARC-NAV-FIT-ABSORBS-CODIRECTIONAL-DECOY, solved after two
motion-based dead-ends (iter9 rate gate, iter11 per-action mode -- both fail
because tu93's marker centroid genuinely moves differently than the body, so no
motion test groups them). Winning insight: the discriminator is SPATIAL
CONTIGUITY. A rigid avatar's colours adjoin each other (tu93's marker is inside
the body); an independent decoy is elsewhere. Fix: keep existing co-shift
detection, then prune any avatar colour not adjoining the largest (body) colour.
tu93 stays EXACTLY {9,4} (zero regression); distant decoy dropped.
Verified: synthetic probe keeps {9,4}+rejects decoy (incl 30% occlusion); tu93
fit {9,4}; tu93 3/3 reproducible; L3 calibration CLEAN unchanged; 31 tests pass.

